    <time>1784534313</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>Security re-vendor: golang.org/x/net 0.55.0 + golang.org/x/crypto 0.52.0
Fixes bsc#1265736, bsc#1266575, bsc#1267120, bsc#1266151. No code changes:
vendored dependency refresh only, upstream tag 1.8.4 unchanged.</comment>
    <requestid>1366554</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="5" vrev="3">
    <srcmd5>3cb6ad28329a4615871682043e756b27</srcmd5>
    <version>1.8.4</version>
    <time>1785265263</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>Two changes:

1. Add a libguestfs-tools subpackage: upstream's
cmd/libguestfs/entrypoint.sh plus the runtime dependency closure of the
libguestfs-tools container image that virtctl guestfs spawns. It
replaces the dead virt-libguestfs-tools-container package, which still
installs the retired unversioned kubevirt-manifests and whose published
image is frozen at kubevirt 1.4.0; the new image flavor goes into
kubevirt-1.8-image.

2. The previous update (SR 1366554) listed CVE-2026-39821 (bsc#1266575)
as fixed by the golang.org/x/net 0.55.0 re-vendor. The idna fix in
0.55.0 is compile-time gated on Unicode 16 tables, which only exist for
go1.27 and newer; our packages build with go1.26, so they do not
contain the active fix and the CVE was not addressed. This update
re-vendors golang.org/x/net to 0.57.0, where the idna fix applies
regardless of the Go toolchain version. Additionally:
- golang.org/x/text 0.37.0 -&gt; 0.40.0: CVE-2026-56852 (bsc#1271661),
  infinite loop on invalid input in unicode/norm.
- golang.org/x/crypto 0.52.0 -&gt; 0.54.0, pulled in by the x/net bump
  (no additional CVE claims).
- Backports of the upstream release-1.8 fixes for CVE-2026-13201
  (bsc#1269093): safepath did not detect a symlink as the last path
  component; includes the related console-socket hardening.

x/net 0.57.0 also contains the fix for CVE-2026-46600 (bsc#1272415) in
dns/dnsmessage; kubevirt does not vendor that package (not affected).

This request supersedes SR 1368109: as requested in its review, the
.changes now retains the full changelog history of the Factory package,
with a single new entry on top covering both changes above.
</comment>
    <requestid>1368214</requestid>
  </revision>
